SITE name="Flint" nav="Docs,Credits,Licence" location="CLI" contact="issues@flint.dev"
THEME family=technical accent=#0ea5e9 mode=light density=tight
SECTION  id=s1  kind=hero  layout=split  tone=quiet
TEXT sec=s1 slot=eyebrow text="CLI"
TEXT sec=s1 slot=title text="Flint [finds] unused indexes in Postgres"
TEXT sec=s1 slot=lede text="This tool scans your database schema to identify bloat. It runs safely inside CI pipelines without touching production data."
ACTION sec=s1 slot=primary label="Read the docs" href="#docs"
ACTION sec=s1 slot=secondary label="View on GitHub" href="#"
MEDIA sec=s1 slot=figure motif=schematic
SECTION  id=s2  kind=features  layout=list  tone=quiet
TEXT sec=s2 slot=eyebrow text="Scans"
TEXT sec=s2 slot=title text="Detects bloat before it slows queries down"
ITEM sec=s2 slot=item title="Schema audit" body="It reads the system catalog to list every index, then compares them against actual query plans."
ITEM sec=s2 slot=item title="CI gatekeeper" body="The scan finishes in under ten seconds so your pipeline never waits for a full database dump."
ITEM sec=s2 slot=item title="Safe mode" body="It only reads metadata and logs findings to stdout without ever executing any SQL statements against live tables."
ITEM sec=s2 slot=item title="Zero config" body="You pass the connection string as an environment variable and it immediately starts reporting on your cluster."
SECTION  id=s3  kind=detail  layout=split  tone=quiet
TEXT sec=s3 slot=eyebrow text="Why Flint"
TEXT sec=s3 slot=title text="The [only] scanner that understands Postgres internals without a dump"
TEXT sec=s3 slot=lede text="Competitors export your schema to JSON and guess at usage. We parse the live system catalog directly, so we know exactly which index is serving zero rows right now."
ACTION sec=s3 slot=primary label="Get the CLI" href="#install"
MEDIA sec=s3 slot=figure motif=schematic
SECTION  id=s4  kind=faq  layout=stack  tone=bold
TEXT sec=s4 slot=eyebrow text="FAQ"
TEXT sec=s4 slot=title text="How does this affect my uptime?"
ITEM sec=s4 slot=item title="No downtime risk" body="The scanner runs as a read-only process that connects to your cluster via the standard port. It never executes write statements, so your application keeps serving requests while we scan."
ITEM sec=s4 slot=item title="What if I have no internet?" body="Flint works entirely offline once installed on your build agent or CI runner. The only time it needs a network connection is when you run the initial install script to fetch the binary from our release page."
ITEM sec=s4 slot=item title="Can this handle huge databases?" body="Yes, because we stream metadata row-by-row instead of loading the whole catalog into memory. A scan on a 50TB cluster with thousands of tables finishes in under two minutes using standard RAM limits."
ITEM sec=s4 slot=item title="What happens to my old indexes?" body="The tool lists them as 'unused' but does not delete anything automatically. You must run the cleanup command manually or schedule it via cron if you want us to drop those files for you after verification."
SECTION  id=s5  kind=cta  layout=stack  tone=quiet
TEXT sec=s5 slot=title text="Run [now] to reclaim storage"
TEXT sec=s5 slot=lede text="Add one line to your CI job and start finding bloat immediately."
ACTION sec=s5 slot=primary label="Install Flint" href="#install"
